Looking for eco friendly wedding rental options in Malaga? Malaga Event Gear's [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) is an AV rental, not a tent, furniture or decor supplier, so its eco credentials are specific to that: fairy light and warm LED ambient lighting instead of older, higher draw fixtures, a reuse model where the same equipment serves event after event instead of being bought once and discarded, and local delivery across Malaga rather than freight shipped in from further afield. For the full picture of what we cover for weddings, see our [wedding rentals](/blog/wedding-rentals/) overview.

## Brief Overview

---

The [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) covers the AV side of your wedding: PA sound for up to 80 guests, fairy light and warm LED ambient lighting, wireless microphones and a live technician, for 650 euros ex VAT. The eco angle here is genuine but specific to AV equipment: efficient LED lighting, gear that gets reused rather than bought and thrown away, and delivery within our own service area rather than long distance freight.

## Key Highlights

---

-   Fairy lights and warm LED strings draw less power than older incandescent or halogen lighting rigs.
-   Rental itself is a reuse model: the same PA system, lights and microphones serve many weddings instead of being bought once per event.
-   Delivery, setup and collection stay local, within Malaga and Granada, rather than shipping equipment long distance, which keeps the trip's transport emissions down.
-   The Wedding Pack is AV equipment only: it does not include tents, furniture, decor or catering, so it cannot make those parts of your wedding eco friendly.

## Where the Wedding Pack Is Genuinely Eco Friendly

LED lighting is the clearest case: the fairy lights and warm LED strings in the Wedding Pack use meaningfully less energy than the incandescent or halogen fixtures still common in older lighting rigs, while giving the same warm ambient glow for a reception. That is a real, measurable difference, not a marketing label.

The rental model itself is the second piece. Every PA system, light and microphone in our catalog gets delivered, collected, checked and sent back out for the next event, rather than being purchased new for a single wedding and discarded afterward. Renting AV equipment is inherently a reuse model, whether or not a supplier markets it that way.

Local delivery is the third piece, and it is worth naming directly. Every kilometer equipment does not have to travel is fuel it does not burn, so keeping our Wedding Pack fleet within Malaga and Granada is a genuine, if modest, reduction in the transport emissions attached to your wedding's AV setup. It also means one delivery and one pickup trip for your entire sound, lighting and microphone setup, rather than a separate van from a tent company, another from a furniture rental and another from catering, each running its own route to the same venue.

